In short:

This role is responsible for identifying opportunities to improve finance processes, eliminating inefficiencies, strengthening controls, standardizing ways of working, and helping finance operate more effectively at scale. This is an ideal opportunity for someone who enjoys solving business problems, challenging the status quo and driving continuous improvement across a complex finance organisation.&nbsp;

Working across Finance team members in all regions and partnering with technology, supply chain, retail and other business functions you will lead process reviews, facilitate workshops, analyse current ways of working and design practical improvements and deliver measurable business value. The scope doesn't stop at fixing today's problems but it contributes to thinking about redesigning the processes that are scalable for the future.&nbsp;

The Senior Specialist - Finance process excellence&nbsp; will report to Head of Finance Automation &amp; Enablement on the Finance operations Excellence team supporting the Finance function across the globe.

&nbsp;

Your Mission:

-&nbsp; Map current (As-is) and future (To-be) processes&nbsp; across Record to Report, Procure to Pay, Order to Cash, Treasury, Tax and Master Data.

-&nbsp; Facilitate stakeholder workshops and analyze operational and financial data to identify trends, pain points, and strategic improvement opportunities

- Apply Lean and continuous improvement techniques to simplify processes. Support root cause analysis using structured problem solving techniques.

-&nbsp; Build and maintain a pipeline of process improvement initiatives. Measure and report realised business benefits.

- Recommend practical improvements based on data analysis that reduce manual effort, improve quality and increase efficiency

-&nbsp; Support implementation of approved improvements and monitor benefits.

&nbsp;

Your Story:

-&nbsp; Proven experience improving end to end finance processes within a complex global organisation (ideally retail).&nbsp;

- Strong knowledge of finance operations, including areas such as Record to Report, Procure to Pay, Order to Cash, Tax, FP&amp;A.

-&nbsp; Excellent process improvement and analytical skills, with experience in process mapping, root cause analysis, Lean or continuous improvement methodologies, and translating insights into practical solutions.

-&nbsp; Strong Stakeholder management and facilitation skills, with the ability to influence, challenge constructively, and build trusted relationships across finance and cross-functional teams.&nbsp;

-&nbsp; Experience with ERP (ideally D365 FO) and tools like Excel/Google sheet, Looker, Miro, Parabola or any workflow builder, AI agents, and process mining tool.

- A collaborative, curious and improvement focussed mindset, with excellent communication skills and a passion for driving operational excellence, governance and sustainable change.

&nbsp;

Your Team:

Join the Finance Operations Excellence (FOX) team at On and become the architect of our global financial future. We don't just maintain the status quo; we are the visionaries redesigning the core business processes that power On's rapid global expansion. By joining FOX, you will be at the forefront of financial innovation, leveraging cutting-edge automation and advanced data governance to transform complex global operations into scalable, frictionless ecosystems. This is a unique opportunity to shape the strategic direction of our finance function, collaborate with cross-functional global teams, and drive high-impact initiatives empowering you to leave a lasting legacy in a dynamic, high-growth environment where your work directly fuels the company's success.

Veeam is the Data and AI Trust Company, specializing in helping organizations ensure their data and AI are fully understood, secured, and resilient to enable the acceleration of safe AI at scale. As the market leader in both data resilience and data security posture management, Veeam is built for the convergence of identity, data, security, and AI risk. Headquartered in Seattle with offices in more than 30 countries, Veeam protects over 550,000 customers worldwide, who trust Veeam to keep their businesses running. Join us as we go fearlessly forward together, growing, learning, and making a real impact for some of the world’s biggest brands.

About the Role

You will own product for the Knowledge Graph and the reporting and analytics experience inside Veeam Data Command&nbsp;Platform&nbsp;(DSPM&nbsp;and AISPM). The graph is where the product's intelligence&nbsp;lives:&nbsp;what sensitive data exists, who can access it, how it moves, and whether the AI&nbsp;working&nbsp;on it can be&nbsp;governed.&nbsp;Actionable&nbsp;dashboards&nbsp;and reporting&nbsp;are how customers see that intelligence, prove their posture to auditors and executives, and decide&nbsp;- and act on -&nbsp;what to fix first. &nbsp;

This is a builder's product role. You will translate a complex graph data model into queries, views, dashboards, and evidence that security, privacy, and governance teams use every day - and you will partner closely with the engineering leader who owns the graph platform and hyperscale lake integrations. &nbsp;

You will set the roadmap, define the metrics that matter, and work AI-first - using agentic tools to prototype, analyze, and ship faster than a traditional PM team. &nbsp;

What You’ll Do

• Own the product vision and roadmap for the Knowledge Graph as a customer-facing capability: the entities, relationships, and insights customers can explore, query, and trust. Partner with engineering on the underlying data modeling (sources, identities, access, classifications, lineage) and translate those decisions into concepts customers&nbsp;actually understand &nbsp;

• Own the dashboard experience end to&nbsp;end:&nbsp;default landing views per&nbsp;persona&nbsp;(CISO, privacy, data governance, security operations), what earns a spot on them, and the path from a top-line number to underlying records in a few clicks. Every widget should&nbsp;answer&nbsp;"so what do I do now?", letting a user assign an owner, open a ticket, launch remediation, tighten a permission, or apply a policy without leaving the view &nbsp;

• Own the widget framework and library (posture scores, top risks,&nbsp;sensitive-data&nbsp;heatmaps, access exposure, AI usage, trend lines) with consistent filtering, time ranges, and drill-through. Enable customization and role-based layouts so customers and internal teams can build, save, share, and default dashboards by role or business unit &nbsp;

• Define the reporting layer: a report builder with saved/shared views, scheduling and subscriptions, and export in the&nbsp;formats&nbsp;enterprises use (PDF, CSV, API). Own audit and evidence packages that hold up for regulators and auditors, with clear scope, timestamps, and provenance back to the graph, and extend reporting coverage to backup and archive estates (Veeam Data Cloud workloads: Microsoft 365, Entra ID, Salesforce) so posture and evidence reflect historical data, not just production &nbsp;

• Drive trending and posture-over-time reporting, including alerting and thresholds, so customers can show risk reduction rather than a single snapshot.&nbsp;Set the bar for data quality and freshness: how recent the numbers are, how coverage gaps are&nbsp;disclosed, and how the product avoids reporting false confidence &nbsp;

• Enable downstream and agent consumption: BI integration, warehouse export, and APIs for customers who want the data in their own stack, plus partnering with the AI Agents team to expose graph queries, findings, and posture metrics as MCP tools

About Neo4j:

Neo4j is the graph intelligence platform that transforms data into knowledge to power the next generation of intelligent applications and AI systems. It includes enterprise-ready knowledge graphs for accurate, explainable, and governed AI; the most comprehensive, trusted, and easy-to-deploy graph capabilities across any environment and data source; and an unmatched ecosystem trusted by 84 of the Fortune 100 and supported by the world’s largest graph community.&nbsp;Intelligence that works. Results that matter.

Built to work everywhere and integrate with everything across every cloud for dynamic, personalized, and autonomous AI systems. We deliver quicker results, contextual knowledge, and solutions that impact customers and employees across the business.

Our Vision:&nbsp;

At Neo4j, we have always strived to help the world make sense of data.&nbsp;&nbsp;

As business, society and knowledge become increasingly connected, our technology promotes innovation by helping organizations to find and understand data relationships. We created, drive and lead the graph database category, and we’re disrupting how organizations leverage their data to innovate and stay competitive.

Role Summary

The Director, Field Engineering Strategy &amp; Execution is the operating partner for the Global Field Engineering organization, embedded within the Office of the CRO's GTM Strategy &amp; Execution function. This role owns the strategic planning, operational cadence, and performance infrastructure that enable the pre-sales/SE (“Field Engineering”) organization to scale efficiently against revenue targets. It translates GTM strategy into Field Engineering execution - capacity planning, coverage models, productivity measurement, tooling, and enablement operations - while acting as the primary strategic advisor to the VP, Global Field Engineering on organizational design and resource allocation.

&nbsp;

This is a hybrid role: formal reporting into GTM Strategy &amp; Execution ensures alignment with company-wide revenue planning and cross-functional GTM systems; the strong dotted line into Global Field Engineering ensures the work is grounded in field reality and has direct influence over how the SE organization is run day to day.

Key Responsibilities

Headcount &amp; Capacity Planning

&nbsp;

• Own the Field Engineering headcount model: current-state coverage, ratio benchmarking (SE:AE, SE:ARR, SE:Account), and forward capacity planning tied to pipeline and bookings targets.

• Partner with Finance and RevOps on annual and in-year headcount requests, backed by data.

• Build and maintain territory/coverage models across segments, regions, and specializations (e.g., vertical or product-line SE pods).

&nbsp;

Performance Operations &amp; Reporting

&nbsp;

• Define and own the Field Engineering KPI framework (e.g., SE utilization, POV win rate, technical win/loss, ramp time, deal-cycle involvement).

• Build and maintain leadership-facing dashboards and QBR materials for the Global Field Engineering organization.

• Run the operating cadence: weekly/monthly business reviews, forecast rollups specific to technical validation stages, and escalation processes for at-risk deals requiring SE intervention.

&nbsp;

Strategic Planning

&nbsp;

• Translate company and GTM Strategy &amp; Execution priorities into Field Engineering execution plans.

• Lead annual planning for the Field Engineering org: goals, org structure, budget inputs, and success metrics.

• Identify structural inefficiencies in field engineering deployment and recommend organizational or process changes.

&nbsp;

Systems, Tools &amp; Process

&nbsp;

• Own the Field Engineering tech stack requirements (CRM data model for SE activity, POV/demo tracking, scheduling and capacity tools) in partnership with RevOps and Sales Systems.

• Standardize and govern SE processes (deal qualification criteria for SE engagement, handoff protocols, POV governance) in partnership with Field

